# Software Architecture for Event-Driven Applications

## Recommended Architecture: **Event-Driven Architecture (EDA)**

### Core Components

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                Event Producers                       │
│  (UI, APIs, Sensors, External Systems)              │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│           Event Bus / Message Broker                 │
│    (Kafka, RabbitMQ, AWS EventBridge, Redis)       │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              Event Processor Layer                   │
│  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐  ┌──────────┐         │
│  │ Handler  │  │ Handler  │  │ Handler  │         │
│  │    A     │  │    B     │  │    C     │         │
│  └──────────┘  └──────────┘  └──────────┘         │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         Business Logic & Services                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Architecture Patterns to Consider

### 1. **Pub/Sub Pattern** (Recommended for most cases)
```javascript
// Event Publisher
class EventPublisher {
  constructor(messageBroker) {
    this.broker = messageBroker;
  }

  publish(eventType, payload) {
    this.broker.publish('events.topic', {
      type: eventType,
      timestamp: Date.now(),
      data: payload
    });
  }
}

// Event Subscriber
class EventSubscriber {
  constructor(messageBroker) {
    this.broker = messageBroker;
    this.handlers = new Map();
  }

  subscribe(eventType, handler) {
    this.handlers.set(eventType, handler);
  }

  listen() {
    this.broker.subscribe('events.topic', (event) => {
      const handler = this.handlers.get(event.type);
      if (handler) handler(event.data);
    });
  }
}
```

### 2. **Event Sourcing Pattern**
Store all changes as a sequence of events
```
Events → Event Store → Projections → Read Models
```

### 3. **CQRS with Events**
Separate read and write operations with event propagation

## Technology Stack Recommendations

### **Message Brokers**

| Technology | Best For | Complexity |
|------------|----------|------------|
| **Apache Kafka** | High-throughput, distributed systems | High |
| **RabbitMQ** | Flexible routing, moderate scale | Medium |
| **AWS EventBridge** | Cloud-native AWS applications | Low |
| **Redis Streams** | Simple pub/sub, real-time | Low |
| **NATS** | Microservices, IoT, cloud-native | Medium |

